{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-25T21:22:04.140Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n**Summary:** Implemented task 4 of change 081.\n\n- **`src/core/trace/scenario-lookup.ts`** (new, 247 lines): `lookupScenario(capability, name, cwd, env)` returns a scenario's outcomes from the effective spec or throws the exact one-message failures. With `OSQ_CHANGE` it merges the living spec with that change's delta via `mergeDelta`; without it, it finds the nearest ancestor holding `openspec/specs` and reconciles the living spec against every active change's ADDED/MODIFIED requirements. Also exports `effectiveScenarios(openspecRoot, changeFolder, capability)` for lint, plus `clearScenarioLookupCache()` and `scenarioSpecReadCount()`. Reads use `node:fs` sync, parses only with `parseDelta`/`mergeDelta`/`parseCapabilitySpec`, lists active changes with `isActiveChangeFolderName`, and caches per openspec root + change folder + capability.\n- **`tests/trace-scenario-lookup.test.ts`** (new): covers all five lookup scenarios plus the lint export, a refused merge, living-spec duplicates, a delta-introduced duplicate, a missing capability, a nested working directory, and single-read caching.\n\nBoth the task verify (`node --import tsx --test tests/trace-scenario-lookup.test.ts`) and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`) pass; line/function budget and biome are clean. Result written to `.run/results/4.md`."}}
